{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved 48.5% accuracy, establishing a modest RNA-only baseline. The single most important structural question is whether the image modality carries complementary or superior signal, since this determines whether the remaining 8 experiments should focus on multimodal fusion or on refining RNA-only representations. Question: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) provides a clean single-modality comparison to config_001—same profile setting, same architectural simplicity, only the modality and encoder differ. If image-only substantially outperforms 48.5%, image is highly informative and multimodal configs become the priority; if it is comparable or worse, RNA improvements (learned encoders, multiprofile) may be more productive. Why this is the best next step: it isolates the modality question with minimal confounding (no fusion, no aggregation), reduces the largest source of uncertainty in the design space, and directly informs allocation of the remaining 8 experiments across the multimodal vs. single-modality branches."
}

